epistemic-boundary-77668850.conceptual_definition:
The formula 
\delta S_{obs} = 0 \iff \text{Adequate Path link}
 represents a fundamental principle in physics, often related to the calculus of variations and action principles. It states that the observable change in a quantity denoted by 
\delta S_{obs}
 is zero if and only if a certain condition, termed 'Adequate Path link', is met. In the context of classical mechanics, 
S_{obs}
 typically represents the 'observed action' along a path. The condition 
\delta S_{obs} = 0
 is the hallmark of a physically realized path, such as the trajectory of a particle or the configuration of a system evolving over time, which extremizes (often minimizes) the action.

physical-structure-37f4b7b8.conceptual_definition:
The formula 
\mathcal{O} = \{ G, \mathcal{M}, \Phi \}
 describes the fundamental components that define the physical structure of a system or object. It posits that any physical structure can be exhaustively characterized by a set of defining elements: the underlying geometric or topological framework, the material composition and distribution of mass-energy, and the field(s) that govern interactions.
